    <!-- The sound driver runs on the 68000 and is driven by two interrupts of the game, which run as they are: the horizontal-blank
         interrupt (0x9432), four times a frame (the game sets the VDP's register 10 to 52), advances the music with a tempo accumulator, and
         the vertical-blank interrupt (0x8F26) does the rest of the sound (volume and pitch changes, fades, the effect parts) after its own
         work, which only reads the controllers when the game's RAM is clear. The Z80 mixes three sampled voices. The game keeps its
         variables in a block addressed by A6 (0xFF0000). 0x9592 loads the Z80's program and 0x9610 sets the sound parts up; the game starts a
         song (0x9622) or an effect (0x963C) by calling a subroutine with A0 pointing at a word that holds the number. The header of the
